--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI RegenEfficiencyPage at web parity: a pure @Observable state holder
(ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable RegenEfficiencyDataSource seam whose method
names mirror the web hooks at the Swift call sites (loadVehicles ← useSelectedVehicle/GET /vehicles;
useRegenEfficiency ← GET /analytics/regen?vehicle_id&start&end; useDrives ← GET /drives?vehicle_id).
Every web useMemo derivation is ported (monthlyTrend = group-by-YYYY-MM → sum kWh + count, sort,
.suffix(12); regenDrives = filter(regenEnergyWh>0).prefix(20); getRegenRatio). Energy / power / distance
convert to the user's unit ONLY at the render boundary via the shared Units facade + RegenEfficiencyFormat
(ADR-005, SI-cutover); the model holds the /analytics/regen + /drives shapes verbatim in SI (Wh, W, m).
The regen roll-up's monthly_avg_regen is read as SI watts (the backend averages avg_power_w in W despite
the legacy _kw JSON alias) and formatted with formatPower at precision 1, exactly as the web does.

The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle + the global VehicleSelect + the
RangePicker date filter; web useRangeState defaultPresetId:'all' → a wide default window) and ALL of the
web's sections:

  GlassPanel1   — RegenHeroSection: the regen-ratio RadialGauge (RegenRatioGauge → TSRadialGauge, tinted
                  by the web regenColor tier green≥25/cyan≥15/amber≥8/red) + the "you've recovered {energy}
                  — ~{charges} free charges" caption.
  GlassPanel2-7 — RegenStatCardsSection (six RegenStatCard tiles): Total Regen, Recovery Rate, Monthly Avg
                  kW, Free Charges (animated count-up), and the two intentionally-unwired Lifetime tiles
                  (web renders an em dash). Adaptive 2-up → 6-up grid.
  Monthly-Regen-Trend — RegenMonthlyTrendSection: TSChartContainer hosting the native Swift Charts
                  TSComposedChart (purple drive-count bars under a green regen-kWh line), a colored legend,
                  the YYYY-MM month axis, and the exportable CSV; the monthlyTrend.count>1 guard shows the
                  container's empty overlay otherwise (panel always visible — never blanked).
  GlassPanel9   — RegenMetricsSection: four proportion bars (Total Regen / Regen Ratio / Monthly Avg /
                  Free Charges) each captioned with its formatted value, plus the info HelpTooltip
                  (RegenHelpButton, a11y label = help.regenEfficiency.iconLabel). The web max() denominators
                  are ported verbatim so the bars read identically to the web.
  GlassPanel10  — RegenDrivesSection: the Date / Distance / Max-Regen / Ratio table of recent regen drives
                  (ratio tinted by the regenColor tier), or the common.noData EmptyState when none.

Adaptive (ADR-002/006): the header, the stat-card grid, and the metrics grid reflow for macOS / iPad
regular width vs. compact iPhone. All copy resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names
(29 new bare regen.* / help.regenEfficiency.iconLabel keys added + help.regenEfficiency.body for the
tooltip; common.noData already present). a11y labels on panels + gauge + chart; Dynamic Type; light/dark
via design tokens (no hardcoded colors/typography). Loading = .redacted skeleton; empty/error/success
modeled by RegenEfficiencyPhase.

Navigation (mirrors the sibling unrouted RouteEfficiencyRouteRegistration; the .driving host is owned by
DriveScorePage): typed RegenEfficiencyLink + .regenEfficiencyDestination() NavigationDestination +
RegenEfficiencyRouteRegistration.make() factory, with deep-link path "/regen-efficiency" → .driving added
to AppRouteParser.aliases (like "/route-efficiency").

Files (apps/apple/Sources/Features/Driving/):
  RegenEfficiencyPageModel.swift          — @Observable model, value types, phase, data-source protocol
  RegenEfficiencyPageModel.Sample.swift   — Sample / Empty / Failing data sources
  RegenEfficiencyFormat.swift             — display-boundary formatters (percent/energy/power/distance/tier)
  RegenEfficiencyPage.swift               — View + header + phase switch + previews
  RegenEfficiencyPage.Sections.swift      — hero / stat-cards / metrics panels + help button
  RegenEfficiencyPage.Charts.swift        — RadialGauge + monthly-trend ChartContainer + ComposedChart
  RegenEfficiencyPage.Table.swift         — per-drive table + RangePicker control + loading skeleton
  RegenEfficiencyRouteRegistration.swift  — typed-link NavigationDestination + factory
Tests (apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Driving/):
  RegenEfficiencyPageModelTests.swift     — 12 state-machine / derivation tests
  RegenEfficiencyFormatTests.swift        — 10 formatter tests
Edited: apps/apple/Sources/App/AppRouteParser.swift (one alias line),
        apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings (30 keys)

