     this blocks the whole app build before compilation (commit a52455f9e "dedupe 11 type collisions"
     renamed the *type* to ScheduledExportsPanelView but missed the *filename*).
  B. Divergent duplicate TYPES (parallel-salvage): TirePressureUnit / TirePressureStatus /
     TirePressureThresholds / TirePressureConvert (dashboard-widgets ⨯ Features/VehicleSystems) and
     HeroStatus (shared-surfaces ⨯ Features/System) — same name, different shapes → module-wide ambiguity.
  C. Local design-token SHADOWS: StatusApiDocsPage.swift redefines enum TSSpacing + enum TSRadius (with
     DIFFERENT radius values), and TeslaAccountPageViews.swift adds `extension TSSpacing { static let x2xl }`
     redeclaring an existing token → `TSSpacing.<token>` ambiguous, cascading into ~312 spurious
     `#Preview` (SwiftUI-vs-UIKit macro) + accessibilityAddTraits/init ambiguities across 113 files.
  D. Duplicate extension method `Double.rounded(toPlaces:)` (LifetimeStatsModels ⨯ WeeklyDigest) →
     invalid redeclaration. A local `struct Vehicle` (SystemStatusModels) shadows KMP `Shared.Vehicle`
     (Int64 id) → `BatteryRadialGaugeModel` String?/Int64? type error.
  E. Pre-existing Swift 6 strict-concurrency violations (SWIFT_STRICT_CONCURRENCY=complete), e.g.
     TeslaAccountPage.swift:54/57/92/228 "sending 'self.viewModel' risks causing data races", plus a
